WORKING COPY: the integration worktree ${ROOT} (branch ashline/aaa). Work only there (never the user's main checkout ${REPO}, never other worktrees except reading their branches via git). Absolute paths for Read/Edit/Write; cd explicitly in Bash.
SERVER: python3 -m http.server PORT --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory ${ROOT} (background) → http://127.0.0.1:PORT/fun/ashline/
BROWSER CHECKS: REDACTED.mjs ASHLINE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:PORT/fun/ashline/ REDACTED${W}-int node tests/<name>.mjs — Chrome needs dangerouslyDisableSandbox: true (also pkill/lsof).
NODE SUITE (from fun/ashline): every tests/*-check.mjs that is a node check (not *browser*, *visual*, camera-check, shadows-check, cargo-check, audio-check, building-animation-check, production-ui-check, browser-check, race-balance, ai-ladder full runs) plus node --test tests/*.test.mjs. Look at docs/ARCHITECTURE.md 'Tests and browser checks' for the current list.
COMMITS: end every commit message with a blank line and: Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Rules: deterministic sim; legacy rules must reproduce legacy behaviour (foundation-check fingerprints); save.js validates every field and old saves load; 2000 units/side stay playable; desktop + touch.`

const reportsText = Object.entries(args.reports || {}).map(([k, v]) => `===== TRACK ${k} REPORTS =====\n${v}`).join('\n\n')

phase('Merge')
const mergeReport = await agent(`${BRIEF}
TASK: merge the ${W} track branches into ashline/aaa in this order: ${args.order.map(k => `ashline/${W}-${k}`).join(', ')}. Use port 8120.
For each branch: git merge --no-ff ashline/${W}-<key> (from ${ROOT}). Resolve every conflict by understanding BOTH sides' intent (read the track reports below and the branch diffs), keeping both features working together — never drop a feature to make a conflict go away, and never keep conflict markers. Shared hot spots: main.js input handlers / frame loop / HUD, index.html, ashline.css, render.js draw(), sim.js step()/stepUnit()/createGame, save.js validators, signals.js UI_SIGNALS, sim.js EVENT_CODES/RULE_OPTIONS, settings.js SETTINGS, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, tests. After EACH merge run the node suite; fix breakages immediately (commit fixes separately with clear messages). After all merges run EVERY browser check in tests/ (list them with ls tests/*.mjs) and every new test the tracks added; fix integration failures (a failure that the track itself reported as pre-existing and unfixable must be justified in your report). Then smoke-test the real game in Chrome with SKIRMISH rules through the actual UI (deploy from the setup screen without pinned rules, build a few structures, train units, fight, open the pause menu/options) on desktop 1440x900 and phone 390x844, checking the console for errors; fix what breaks. Take screenshots of the integrated game (base, battle, sidebar, pause/options) and look at them.
Track reports:
${reportsText}
Return: merge log (conflicts and how each was resolved), fixes made, full test results (every check: pass/fail), console errors found, screenshot paths, and remaining problems.`, { label: `${W}:merge`, phase: 'Merge' })

phase('Glue')
const glueReport = await agent(`${BRIEF}
The ${W} tracks were just merged into ashline/aaa. Merge report:
---
${mergeReport}
---
TASK: cross-track glue and contract audit (port 8120).
1. Enumerate every sim EVENT_CODE and UI signal code: where it is emitted and where it is consumed (announcer/sound/toasts/pings/comms/cameo NEW pulse, etc.). Wire every missing link that makes sense (e.g. announcer lines for mechanics events like crates/regrowth/stances/radar/production hold; FX for crushed infantry; cursor states for new order modes; tooltips/lock reasons for tech levels; AI use of new mechanics where cheap). Remove dead reserved codes only if clearly unused by later waves (keep superweapon/aircraft/capture/mission reservations).
2. Every setting in settings.js is wired and does what its label says; every rule key in RULE_OPTIONS is honoured and exposed in the briefing Rules panel if implemented.
3. Keyboard map: no two features bind the same key; the in-game field guide/controls list and help texts reflect all new controls (keep them concise).
4. docs/ARCHITECTURE.md: consolidate the per-track appended sections into a coherent document (no duplication, up-to-date tables).
${args.extraGlue || ''}
Run the node suite and all browser checks; commit. Return a report of the audit table (code → emitters → consumers), what you wired, and test results.`, { label: `${W}:glue`, phase: 'Glue' })

phase('QA')
const FINDINGS = {
  type: 'object',
  properties: {
    findings: { type: 'array', items: { type: 'object', properties: {
      severity: { type: 'string', enum: ['blocker', 'major', 'minor'] },
      area: { type: 'string' }, file: { type: 'string' }, line: { type: 'integer' },
      problem: { type: 'string' }, evidence: { type: 'string' }, fix: { type: 'string' },
    }, required: ['severity', 'area', 'problem', 'evidence', 'fix'] } },
    summary: { type: 'string' },
  },
  required: ['findings', 'summary'],
}
const QA_BASE = `${BRIEF}
You are a QA reviewer. Do NOT modify tracked files (write scratch scripts under /tmp/claude-501/qa-${W}-*). The integrated build is on ashline/aaa (${ROOT}). Glue report:
---
${glueReport}
---
Report only real, verified problems with evidence (commands, screenshots you looked at, console output).`
const LENSES = [
  { key: 'play', port: 8141, text: `LENS: a human player. Using Playwright as a player would (real clicks/keys/touch, SKIRMISH rules via the setup screen, both factions), play several minutes of a match at 1x/2x speed: build a base through the sidebar, harvest, train an army, use stances/waypoints/force-fire/control groups/cursors/radar, fight the AI, win or lose, look at the result screen; repeat on phone 390x844 with touch. Report anything broken, confusing, ugly or un-AAA (with screenshots), plus console errors.` },
  { key: 'fog', port: 8142, text: `LENS: fog-of-war honesty and fairness. Try hard to find any channel that reveals hidden enemy state: rendering (VFX, wrecks, light, shake, smoke), audio (spatial sounds, ambience, announcer), comms log/pings/minimap/radar, cursors/tooltips (hovering hidden units), stats mid-game, AI cheating (decisions from hidden info). Build targeted Playwright/node probes (pixel diffs with a hidden vs absent enemy, signal logs).` },
  { key: 'perf', port: 8143, text: `LENS: performance and stability. Measure frame time and sim step time in large battles (300+ and 1000+ units on vast maps, heavy VFX, both factions) at 1x and 2x speed; memory growth over a long match (events/effects/decals/particles/audio voices); save size at scale and save/load round trips of complex states (all new fields); long AI-vs-AI soak (no exceptions, no NaN positions, no stuck units). Report regressions with numbers.` },
  { key: 'visual', port: 8144, text: `LENS: art director for a AAA classic RTS. Take a screenshot tour: setup screen, loading, early base, mid-game base (both factions), big battle with explosions/fire/wrecks, destroyed base, lava/terrain, night-like dark areas, sidebar/cameos/tooltips, pause/options, comms/announcer strip, minimap, mobile layouts, min and max zoom. Judge against C&C/RA/TS polish and AGENTS.md readability rules: units distinguishable, UI cohesive and legible, effects impactful but not obscuring. Report concrete, fixable issues (specific colours/sizes/timings) with screenshot paths.` },
  { key: 'saves', port: 8145, text: `LENS: save/load and determinism. Create games with every rule combination (legacy, skirmish, crates, regrowth, tech levels, start modes, victory modes, AI doctrines/difficulties), advance them with combat, stances, waypoints, held production, crates picked up, regrowth happening; save/load round-trip through save.js and continue both copies for 120+ s and compare full state; check old-save fixtures (from commit 37c177c) still load; check legacy fingerprints (foundation-check) and that race-balance legacy runs reproduce docs/BALANCE.md's first calibration match result.` },
]
const qa = await parallel(LENSES.map(l => () => agent(`${QA_BASE}\nUse port ${l.port}.\n${l.text}\n${args.extraQA || ''}`, { label: `${W}:qa-${l.key}`, phase: 'QA', schema: FINDINGS }).then(r => r && ({ lens: l.key, ...r }))))
const findings = qa.filter(Boolean).flatMap(r => r.findings.map(f => ({ lens: r.lens, ...f })))
log(`QA findings: ${findings.length} (${findings.filter(f => f.severity === 'blocker').length} blockers, ${findings.filter(f => f.severity === 'major').length} major)`)

phase('Fix')
let fixReport = 'No QA findings.'
if (findings.length) {
  fixReport = await agent(`${BRIEF}
QA reviewers reported these findings on the integrated ashline/aaa (JSON):
${JSON.stringify(findings, null, 1)}
Deduplicate, verify each, and fix every real blocker and major, plus minors that are cheap and safe. Use port 8120. Re-run the node suite and ALL browser checks; commit (group related fixes). Return a table of findings with outcome (fixed / not reproducible / deferred + reason) and the final full test results.`, { label: `${W}:fix`, phase: 'Fix' })
}
return { mergeReport, glueReport, qa, fixReport }

